      "headline": "Freelance Composer at Self-employed",
      "about": "I write music for films, games, television, commercials, and various music libraries. I also release music under the name Watermark High.\n\nAlthough I'm musically self-taught and have about two decades' experience performing and writing, I earned my Master's degree in \"Professional Media Composition\" from the University of Chichester / Thinkspace in 2023. I also completed my studies in game audio implementation using Wwise at the School of Video Game Audio in 2019, under the guidance of industry veteran Leonard Paul.\n\nMy debut feature documentary score was for \"Sustainable Nation.\" My music has also been featured in various independent international film projects, including the documentary \"Make,\" as well as in several video game documentaries. It has even made its way into reality TV shows like \"Keeping Up With The Kardashians\" and has been used by numerous online content creators.\n\nI've had the privilege of soundtracking advertising projects for brands such as Microsoft, adidas, Absolut Vodka, Samsung, Fila, Cadillac, New Balance, and many others.",
